<description>Itadakimasu (いただきます) is a Japanese word meaning “I humbly receive.” Said before a meal in Japan, often as thanks to everything that made it possible. Who helped bring today&#x27;s food to you? From GLOBAL INNER DIVINE, a small studio in Japan.</description>
